 "result": "This looks consistent. Adding one message per date-relevant channel gives each an observable `ts` (a field the API definitely returns and the solver is expected to convert to a date) that reflects its true creation timeframe, without changing the formal query logic.\n\n**Summary of fix:** `A:Conversation.created_at` apparently isn't observable through the replica's channel reads in this environment, so `C_LATE`'s distinguishing date (\"2026-03-04\") never showed up in any read. I added a short kickoff message to `C_LATE` (and, for consistency/robustness, to `C_ATLAS`, `C_SIX`, `C_OWNER`, and `C_PLAIN`) timestamped at each channel's intended creation time, so the solver can read the channel's timeframe via message `ts` (a field `conversations.history` reliably returns) instead of relying on the unobservable `created` field. The reference query and decoy mutations are unchanged.",
